```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Agent harness engineers designing system-prompt envelopes (e.g., Claude Code–style <env> heads) who place per-session inert identifiers (session_uuid) before the shared tool-schema prefix; also Codex-style harnesses where the measurement confirms no volatile-token ceiling exists and optimization effort should be directed elsewhere.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-simulation only: token-counting capacity-sim on reconstructed CC heads (Mac CPU stdlib, gpt2 tokenizer) reports +32,040 tok (+28.1%) recompute saved at cap=0.30 and hit Δ +0.283, but this is an UPPER BOUND (FIX-2) with prompt-output equivalence not demonstrated at L0; no production GPU serving, no wall-clock, no measurement against a paged kernel (vLLM PagedAttention 2309.06180, SGLang RadixAttention 2312.07104) that is already fast. The CC gap (realized_frac 0.082, ~92% relative gap) is real on the reconstructed trace but collapses to a TOP-1 lever (session_uuid 93.8% of marginal mass, FIX-4 domination) with zero semantic collision cost (0.000), matching published Anthropic/OpenAI cache guidance—i.e., a harness-design fix, not a serving-system innovation. Codex realized_frac 0.993 is a CLEAN KILL, proving volatile tokens are not a bottleneck when a byte-identical base_instructions block (~6.6k tok) fronts the prefix.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [1] Instrument-specific UPPER BOUND: CC head is RECONSTRUCTED (real in-trace values but documented <env> format), magnitude depends on field ordering, not a fleet-universal constant. [2] No production validation: token-counting sim only, no end-to-end latency/throughput on GPU, no verification that masking preserves model output semantics. [3] Trivial fix replicates vendor docs: relocating session_id to suffix is already recommended by Anthropic/OpenAI cache guidance (packet discloses), so adoption is a one-line harness change, not a research artifact. [4] Limited generality: Codex negative shows the ceiling disappears with a well-ordered harness; the 12-class taxonomy has 9/12 classes contributing zero for CC, and the joint-masking interaction (52% of gap not captured by marginals) complicates practical implementation.
RATIONALE: CC realized_frac 0.082 vs canonicalized-max 577.6 tok demonstrates a real gap on the reconstructed trace, but RE-A1 is degenerate (session_uuid 93.8% marginal, top-3 share 1.000 with FIX-4 flag) and RE-A3 CI95 [0.736,1.000] reflects taxonomy uncertainty; HHI 0.020 confirms fleet-wide property but does not overcome the UPPER-BOUND caveat. Codex realized_frac 0.993 with -549 tok (-2.7%) at cap=0.30 is an honest negative, actionable as "do not waste effort on volatile-token normalization if your harness already shares a byte-identical prefix." The +28.1% recompute saved is not a production win against SGLang RadixAttention (2312.07104) or vLLM APC (2309.06180); it is a simulation of what a correctly ordered harness would achieve, which is already achievable by following existing vendor guidance.
```
